 PROMPT = """A customer of an online shop searched for: {query}
 
-Pick up to {limit} products from the list that best match the search, best first.
-Answer with one product per line, as: ID | one short reason, addressed to the customer
+Pick up to {limit} products from the list that genuinely suit the search, best first.
+Only pick a product if it is what the customer is looking for, or a close fit for it.
+Do not pick products just because they are popular, cheap or highly rated. If nothing
+in the list suits the search (for example the shop does not sell that kind of thing),
+pick nothing: answer with the single word NONE.
+Otherwise answer with one product per line, as: ID | one short reason, addressed to
+the customer, explaining how the product fits their search
 
 Products (ID | name | price | rating out of 5):
 {products}
